"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Hessian is singular. Try providing starting values or using fewer covariates</span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\"><br></span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">But otherwise it appears as if the model runs normally. But the output is as follows: </span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\"><br></span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">\r\n\r\n<span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">Occupancy:\r\n                        Estimate SE  z P(&gt;|z|)\r\n(Intercept)             3.99e-06 NA NA      NA\r\nVegetation              2.83e-07 NA NA      NA\r\nDistance_National_Park  1.89e-01 NA NA      NA\r\nDistance_Shore          3.50e-03 NA NA      NA\r\nDistance_Village        5.43e-03 NA NA      NA\r\nDistance_Cages          3.83e-02 NA NA      NA\r\nCages_Present_Binary    1.47e-06 NA NA      NA\r\nWater_Depth            -8.26e-05 NA NA      NA\r\nFishing_Intensity       2.19e-06 NA NA      NA\r\n\r\nDetection:\r\n            Estimate SE  z P(&gt;|z|)\r\n(Intercept)    2.440 NA NA      NA\r\nStart_Time    -0.407 NA NA      NA\r\nDuration       1.582 NA NA      NA\r\nDay           -1.328 NA NA      NA\r\nSurvey_Team    1.194 NA NA      NA\r\nLength        -1.658 NA NA      NA</span></span></span>\r\n\r\nIs there any particular reason why SE, z, &amp; <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:13.3333px\">P(&gt;|z|) all appear as NA? And is there a way to fix this? </span>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</span></span></span></div>"
