   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nDear Dani,</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nread the red stuff, especially the second sentence. You probably try to squeeze out too many estimates from not enough information. How many sites and how many repeated measurements per site do you have ?</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nHave you tried building up your model step by step, starting with a simple models with few covariates and then adding in more and more ? You can then use estimates of the simpler models as initial values for the next step in the progression from simple to complex\r\n model.<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nBest regards --- Marc<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<hr style=\"display:inline-block;width:98%\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" style=\"font-size:11pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><b>From:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unma...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unma...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; on behalf of Daniel Villar &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">daniel....@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Thursday, January 4, 2024 03:34<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> unmarked &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unma...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [unmarked] Why are SE, z, &amp; P(&gt;|z|) appearing as NA in my model output</font>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div></div>"
